# Unit 22 单词



## project
- **音标**: /ˈprɑːdʒekt/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 项目；投射；预测
- **例句**: The project is expected to be completed by December.
- **近义词**: plan, scheme, forecast
- **派生词**: projection (n.), projector (n.)

## prominent
- **音标**: /ˈprɑːmɪnənt/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 突出的；著名的
- **例句**: He is a prominent figure in the field of science.
- **近义词**: distinguished, notable, famous
- **派生词**: prominence (n.), prominently (adv.)

## promote
- **音标**: /prəˈmoʊt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 促进；提升；推广
- **例句**: The company promoted him to senior manager.
- **近义词**: advance, encourage, boost
- **派生词**: promotion (n.), promoter (n.), promotional (adj.)

## prompt
- **音标**: /prɑːmpt/
- **词性**: adj. v. n.
- **释义**: 迅速的；促使；提示
- **例句**: Thank you for your prompt reply.
- **近义词**: quick, swift, trigger
- **派生词**: promptly (adv.), promptness (n.)

## prone
- **音标**: /proʊn/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 易于…的；俯卧的
- **例句**: Children are prone to catching colds in winter.
- **近义词**: susceptible, inclined, likely
- **派生词**: proneness (n.)

## proportion
- **音标**: /prəˈpɔːrʃn/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 比例；部分；均衡
- **例句**: A large proportion of the budget goes to education.
- **近义词**: ratio, percentage, share
- **派生词**: proportional (adj.), proportionally (adv.), disproportionate (adj.)

## propose
- **音标**: /prəˈpoʊz/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 提议；建议；求婚
- **例句**: He proposed a new plan to the board.
- **近义词**: suggest, recommend, offer
- **派生词**: proposal (n.), proposition (n.)

## prospect
- **音标**: /ˈprɑːspekt/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 前景；展望；可能性
- **例句**: The prospects for economic growth are good.
- **近义词**: outlook, possibility, chance
- **派生词**: prospective (adj.), prospector (n.)

## prosper
- **音标**: /ˈprɑːspər/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 繁荣；兴旺
- **例句**: The business has prospered under new management.
- **近义词**: thrive, flourish, succeed
- **派生词**: prosperity (n.), prosperous (adj.)

## protest
- **音标**: /ˈproʊtest/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 抗议；反对
- **例句**: Thousands of people joined the protest march.
- **近义词**: objection, demonstration, complain
- **派生词**: protester (n.), protestation (n.)

## provide
- **音标**: /prəˈvaɪd/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 提供；供应；规定
- **例句**: The hotel provides free Wi-Fi for guests.
- **近义词**: supply, offer, furnish
- **派生词**: provision (n.), provider (n.), provided (conj.)

## provoke
- **音标**: /prəˈvoʊk/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 激怒；引起；挑衅
- **例句**: His remarks provoked an angry response.
- **近义词**: irritate, trigger, incite
- **派生词**: provocation (n.), provocative (adj.), provocatively (adv.)

## pursue
- **音标**: /pərˈsuː/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 追求；从事；追赶
- **例句**: She decided to pursue a career in medicine.
- **近义词**: follow, chase, seek
- **派生词**: pursuit (n.), pursuer (n.)

## qualify
- **音标**: /ˈkwɑːlɪfaɪ/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 使合格；有资格；限定
- **例句**: Her experience qualifies her for the job.
- **近义词**: certify, entitle, meet requirements
- **派生词**: qualification (n.), qualified (adj.), qualitative (adj.)

## quote
- **音标**: /kwoʊt/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 引用；报价
- **例句**: She quoted a famous line from Shakespeare.
- **近义词**: cite, mention, price
- **派生词**: quotation (n.), quotable (adj.)

## radical
- **音标**: /ˈrædɪkl/
- **词性**: adj. n.
- **释义**: 根本的；激进的
- **例句**: The company needs radical changes to survive.
- **近义词**: drastic, extreme, fundamental
- **派生词**: radically (adv.), radicalism (n.)

## random
- **音标**: /ˈrændəm/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 随机的；任意的
- **例句**: The numbers were selected at random.
- **近义词**: haphazard, arbitrary, chance
- **派生词**: randomly (adv.), randomness (n.)

## range
- **音标**: /reɪndʒ/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 范围；系列；山脉
- **例句**: The hotel offers a wide range of services.
- **近义词**: scope, variety, extent
- **派生词**: ranger (n.)

## rank
- **音标**: /ræŋk/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 等级；排名；排列
- **例句**: She ranks first in her class.
- **近义词**: position, grade, status
- **派生词**: ranking (n. adj.)

## rapid
- **音标**: /ˈræpɪd/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 迅速的；快的
- **例句**: The city has experienced rapid growth in recent years.
- **近义词**: fast, quick, swift
- **派生词**: rapidly (adv.), rapidity (n.)

## rare
- **音标**: /rer/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 稀有的；罕见的
- **例句**: This is a rare species of bird.
- **近义词**: scarce, uncommon, unusual
- **派生词**: rarely (adv.), rarity (n.)

## rate
- **音标**: /reɪt/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 比率；速度；评价
- **例句**: The unemployment rate has decreased this year.
- **近义词**: ratio, speed, pace
- **派生词**: rating (n.), overrate (v.), underrated (adj.)

## rational
- **音标**: /ˈræʃnəl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 理性的；合理的
- **例句**: We need a rational approach to solving this problem.
- **近义词**: logical, reasonable, sensible
- **派生词**: rationality (n.), rationalize (v.), irrational (adj.)

## raw
- **音标**: /rɔː/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 生的；未加工的；原始的
- **例句**: Don't eat raw meat; it might contain bacteria.
- **近义词**: uncooked, unprocessed, natural
- **派生词**: rawness (n.)

## react
- **音标**: /riˈækt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 反应；起化学反应
- **例句**: How did she react to the news?
- **近义词**: respond, reply, act
- **派生词**: reaction (n.), reactionary (n. adj.), reactive (adj.)

## realistic
- **音标**: /ˌriːəˈlɪstɪk/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 现实的；实际的
- **例句**: We need to set realistic goals for the project.
- **近义词**: practical, pragmatic, sensible
- **派生词**: realistically (adv.), realism (n.), realist (n.)

## realm
- **音标**: /relm/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 领域；王国
- **例句**: He has made significant contributions to the realm of science.
- **近义词**: domain, field, kingdom

## reasonable
- **音标**: /ˈriːznəbl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 合理的；公道的
- **例句**: The prices at this restaurant are very reasonable.
- **近义词**: fair, sensible, logical
- **派生词**: reasonably (adv.), unreasonable (adj.)

## rebel
- **音标**: /ˈrebl/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 叛乱者；反叛
- **例句**: The rebels fought against the government.
- **近义词**: insurgent, revolutionary, defy
- **派生词**: rebellion (n.), rebellious (adj.)

## recall
- **音标**: /rɪˈkɔːl/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 回忆；召回；收回
- **例句**: I can't recall his name at the moment.
- **近义词**: remember, recollect, retrieve
- **派生词**: recallable (adj.)

## recession
- **音标**: /rɪˈseʃn/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 衰退；萧条
- **例句**: The country is going through a severe recession.
- **近义词**: downturn, slump, depression
- **派生词**: recessive (adj.)
